-- title:
--   Node ring base-changed to a layer of constants
-- statement:
--   Let $L \subseteq F$ be fields ($F$ an $L$-algebra), let $C' \subseteq L$ be a subring that is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and let $\varpi' \in C'$ be irreducible. Let $N_0 \subseteq F$ be a Noetherian local subring containing the image of $C'$, such that: every $g \in N_0$ differs from the image of some $o \in C'$ (itself lying in $N_0$) by a non-unit of $N_0$; for every $n$, every $C'$-linearly independent $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to L$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to N_0$ with $\sum_i c_i \cdot a_i = 0$ in $F$ one has $a \equiv 0$; the image of $\varpi'$ is a non-unit of $N_0$; and $\mathrm{ringKrullDim}\,N_0 \ge 2$. Let $C'' \subseteq L$ be a subring with $C' \le C''$, again a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with irreducible $\varpi''$, and suppose $\varpi' = v\,\varpi''^{\,e}$ for some $e \ge 1$ and some $v$ with $v, v^{-1} \in C''$. Suppose there is a subring $R$ with $C' \le R \le C''$ which is module-finite over $C'$ and such that every $c \in C''$ is of the form $r/s$ with $r, s \in R$, $s \ne 0$, $s^{-1} \in C''$. Let $T''$ be the subring of $F$ generated by $N_0$ together with the image of $C''$, and let $\mathfrak{M} \subseteq T''$ be the ideal spanned by the elements of $T''$ equal to a non-unit of $N_0$ together with the element equal to the image of $\varpi''$. Then $\mathfrak{M}$ is maximal, and there is a subring $TL \subseteq F$ consisting exactly of those $f \in F$ with $f b = a$ for some $a, b \in T''$ with $b \notin \mathfrak{M}$ (the localisation of $T''$ at $\mathfrak{M}$ inside $F$), which is Noetherian and local, contains $N_0$, and satisfies: non-units of $N_0$ stay non-units in $TL$; every $g \in TL$ differs from the image of some $o \in C''$ (lying in $TL$) by a non-unit; granted that the image of $\varpi''$ lies in $TL$, the maximal ideal of $TL$ is contained in the sum of the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $N_0$ and the ideal generated by that image of $\varpi''$; and $\mathrm{ringKrullDim}\,TL \ge 2$.
--
--   This is the local algebra at the special point of the base change of an ordinary double point along a finite extension of discretely valued constants, packaged so that the hypotheses on $N_0$ (constants plus non-units, $C'$-linear disjointness, dimension at least two) are reproduced for the layer ring $TL$, allowing the construction to be iterated. Note that $T''$ itself need not be local, which is why the localisation at the explicitly described ideal $\mathfrak{M}$ appears; the result feeds the ascent of the crossing model to a layer and the analysis of primes of the node chart.
-- source:
